IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cp1-nouns`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, Part I, Division B -- sections 11.1 and 11.2: THE CONTRIBUTION RATES.
--
-- For the years 1966 to 1986 the Act states the rate itself (1.8% for employees and employers, 3.6% for
-- self-employed persons). From 1987 the rate is "as set out in Schedule 1", and the first and second additional
-- rates (2019 on) "as set out in Schedule 2". The Schedules are at the end of the Act and belong to piece cp6; this
-- module takes the figure the Schedule sets as a plain input. A rate is a fraction (5.95% is 0.0595).
--
-- The keel's `Contributing capacity` and `Tier` name the three capacities and the three tiers.

§ `Division B -- Calculation of Contributions`

§§ `Section 11.1 -- the contribution rate`

-- src:321 | Contribution rate — 1966 to 1986
-- src:322 | 11.1 (1) The contribution rate for the years 1966 to 1986 is:
-- src:323 | (a) for employees, 1.8% of contributory wages and salaries;
-- src:324 | (b) for employers, 1.8% of contributory wages and salaries; and
-- src:325 | (c) for self-employed persons, 3.6% of contributory self-employed earnings.
@ref Act s 11.1(1) (src:321-325)
GIVEN capacity IS A `Contributing capacity`
      year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 11.1(1) — the contribution rate for the years 1966 to 1986` capacity year MEANS
    IF year AT LEAST 1966 AND year AT MOST 1986
    THEN JUST (CONSIDER capacity
               WHEN `contributing as an employee` THEN 1.8%
               WHEN `contributing as an employer` THEN 1.8%
               WHEN `contributing as a self-employed person` THEN 3.6%)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:326 | Contribution rates after 1986
-- src:327 | (2) The contribution rate for employees, employers and self-employed persons for 1987 and subsequent years is as set out in Schedule 1, as amended from time to time under section 113.1.
-- out of range: Schedule 1 (piece cp6; lines 3101 to 3122 of the Act) sets the rate for each year from 1987.
@ref Act s 11.1(2) (src:326-327)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the rate set out in Schedule 1 for the capacity and the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 11.1(2) — the contribution rate for 1987 and subsequent years` year `the rate set out in Schedule 1 for the capacity and the year` MEANS
    IF year AT LEAST 1987
    THEN JUST `the rate set out in Schedule 1 for the capacity and the year`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The contribution rate of section 2(1) "contribution rate": the rate that section 11.1 gives for a capacity and a year.
@ref Act s 11.1 (src:321-327)
GIVEN capacity IS A `Contributing capacity`
      year IS A NUMBER
      `the rate set out in Schedule 1 for the capacity and the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 11.1 — the contribution rate for a capacity and a year` capacity year `the rate set out in Schedule 1 for the capacity and the year` MEANS
    IF year LESS THAN 1987
    THEN `s 11.1(1) — the contribution rate for the years 1966 to 1986` capacity year
    ELSE `s 11.1(2) — the contribution rate for 1987 and subsequent years` year `the rate set out in Schedule 1 for the capacity and the year`

§§ `Section 11.2 -- the first additional and the second additional contribution rates`

-- src:330 | First and second additional contribution rates
-- src:331 | 11.2 The first additional contribution rate and the second additional contribution rate for employees, employers and self-employed persons for 2019 and subsequent years is as set out in Schedule 2, as amended from time to time under section 113.1.
-- out of range: Schedule 2 (piece cp6; lines 3123 to 3137 of the Act) sets each of the two rates for each year from 2019.
@ref Act s 11.2 (src:330-331)
GIVEN tier IS A Tier
      year IS A NUMBER
      `the rate set out in Schedule 2 for the tier, the capacity and the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 11.2 — the first or second additional contribution rate for a tier and a year` tier year `the rate set out in Schedule 2 for the tier, the capacity and the year` MEANS
    CONSIDER tier
    WHEN `the base tier` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE
        IF year AT LEAST 2019
        THEN JUST `the rate set out in Schedule 2 for the tier, the capacity and the year`
        ELSE NOTHING
